  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Myomo’s core wearable robotics business is gaining momentum, with MyoPro orders accelerating and nearly half of revenue now coming from recurring patient sources, signaling a shift toward more predictable, annuity-like income. Demand for upper-limb paralysis solutions is growing without any noted macro, regulatory, or competitive disruptions. The company is successfully expanding market access and deepening its recurring revenue base, though the Q4 period previously highlighted margin pressure.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership articulated a clear 2026 plan centered on recurring revenue growth, market access expansion, operating leverage, and innovation. Early execution is evident: first-quarter actions delivered broader gross margins, lower expenses, and a narrower loss, reversing the cost pressures seen in late 2025. By beating internal targets and demonstrating disciplined spending, management is beginning to rebuild credibility and showing it can translate demand into improved operational efficiency.",
